# .image-version-ignore — files whose `ghcr.io/vibeic/vibeic-eda:X.Y.Z` mentions
# are HISTORY, not live install pointers, so the drift-net must not flag them
# when VERSION advances. One glob per line (matched against basename AND repo-rel
# path; see sync_image_version.py::_matches). HISTORY_GLOBS already covers
# FIX_STATUS / CHANGELOG / *ROADMAP* / *_STATUS.md.
#
# Benchmark RESULT.md files record WHICH image a PAST clean-room run used (its
# tool-substitution disclosure). That tag is an immutable record of that run —
# never a live pointer that should track VERSION — so ignore them.
#
# BOUNDED BY LOCATION, not by NAME. This was the bare basename `RESULT.md`, and
# `_matches` tries the basename against every path in the repo — so a
# `docs/RESULT.md` or a plugin `RESULT.md` written next year would be silently
# exempted from the drift-net, by nothing but its filename. MEASURED at the time
# of this change: all 56 tracked RESULT.md are run records (55 under
# benchmark-data/, 1 under benchmark_external/), so the two globs below cover
# exactly today's population and stop covering anything that leaves it. What
# makes a file a record is WHERE it is, not what it is called.
benchmark-data/*/RESULT.md
benchmark_external/*/RESULT.md
# Sign-off reports are the same: they record the exact toolchain a SPECIFIC
# tapeout/sign-off run used (e.g. a commercial-PDK SPM sign-off on 0.2.16 / yosys 0.66-vibeic).
# 0.2.17 ships yosys 0.67, so bumping the tag would misstate that run — history.
*SIGNOFF*.md

